### Talk Reviewer (Lab 2)
# TalkReviewController - Prompt template + system message + structured output
POST http://localhost:8080/talks/review
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "AI for Java Developers",
  "description": "Java developers don't need Python to build AI apps. In this hands-on workshop you'll build a Spring Boot app with Spring AI, one feature at a time: chat, prompt templates, structured output, tools, and MCP."
}

###

### Talk Coach (Lab 3), 1. Share your talk
# TalkCoachController - memory + SimpleLoggerAdvisor + a word count tool. Plain text body.
POST http://localhost:8080/talks/coach
Content-Type: text/plain

Here's my talk. Title: AI Is the Future. Description: Everyone is talking about AI. Come learn why AI matters.

### Talk Coach, 2. Memory remembers your talk
POST http://localhost:8080/talks/coach
Content-Type: text/plain

Make the title punchier.

### Talk Coach, 3. The model calls countWords
POST http://localhost:8080/talks/coach
Content-Type: text/plain

How many words is my description? Is it under 100 words?

### Talk Coach, 4. A new conversation starts empty
POST http://localhost:8080/talks/coach?conversation=new
Content-Type: text/plain

What's my talk title?

###

# ============================================================================
# 5. MEMORY & STATEFUL CONVERSATIONS
# ============================================================================

### Stateful Chat - First Message
# StatefulController - Start conversation with name introduction
GET http://localhost:8080/memory?message=My name is John and I like programming

###

### Stateful Chat - Follow-up
# StatefulController - Follow-up question (remembers context from previous message)
GET http://localhost:8080/memory?message=What is my name?

###

### Stateful Chat - Another Follow-up
# StatefulController - Another follow-up (tests memory persistence)
GET http://localhost:8080/memory?message=What did I say I like?

###

######## Short-term memory: one conversation, replayed by the advisor ########

### S1. Tell it your name
# ShortTermMemoryController
POST http://localhost:8080/memory/short-term/s1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Hi, my name is Maria. Answer in one short sentence."
}

### S2. Ask for it back. It remembers, because the advisor replays S1.
POST http://localhost:8080/memory/short-term/s1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "What's my name?"
}

### S3. Look inside the repository: 4 messages (2 user, 2 assistant)
GET http://localhost:8080/memory/short-term/s1

### S4. A new conversation ID starts empty. It has no idea.
POST http://localhost:8080/memory/short-term/s2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "What's my name?"
}

### S5. Restart the app, then look again: empty. The default repository is a Map in the JVM.
GET http://localhost:8080/memory/short-term/s1

######## Long-term memory: Markdown notes the model writes, one folder per user ########
# Start clean: rm -rf memories. Keep the memories/ folder open in the IDE. The files appear on L1.

### L1. Conversation 1: Maria tells us about her trip. Watch memories/maria/ appear.
# LongTermMemoryController
POST http://localhost:8080/memory/long-term/maria
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "conversationId": "trip",
  "message": "I'm traveling to Portugal next week. Please text me about anything, don't email."
}

### L2. Conversation 2, new conversation ID: the model reads her files and recalls Portugal and texting
POST http://localhost:8080/memory/long-term/maria
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "conversationId": "packing",
  "message": "What should I pack for my trip? And how will you remind me?"
}

### L3. Another user, same question: James's tools only reach memories/james/
POST http://localhost:8080/memory/long-term/james
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "conversationId": "packing",
  "message": "What should I pack for my trip? And how will you remind me?"
}

### L4. Forget Maria: her folder and her conversations are deleted
DELETE http://localhost:8080/memory/long-term/maria

### L5. Ask again in conversation 2: nothing is recalled
POST http://localhost:8080/memory/long-term/maria
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "conversationId": "packing",
  "message": "What should I pack for my trip? And how will you remind me?"
}

